        {
          "ruleId": "refund-to-sender",
          "ruleIndex": 27,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Refunds go back to the address the payment came from. The Bitcoin developer guide calls this very unsafe: the payment may have come from an exchange or a shared wallet that cannot tell which of its users the refund is for, and asks the payer for a refund address instead. Fix: Ask the payer for a refund address (destination \"customer-provided\") instead of sending a refund to the sending address."
          },
